Subject: Powerful When Needed: list the Meta chords the machine binds; drop the Activities card

The Keyboard Shortcuts card builds each of its rows from
globalShortcutTexts() for the action the row teaches, and leaves out a row
whose action has no chord, so it names only chords this machine binds and
follows a rebound action to its new chord. The Activities card is removed:
KDOS ships no activities interface and binds no activity-switcher chord.

